      "version": "2.3.7.9"
    },
    "description": "Returns the onboarding history for a specific PnP device identified by serial number. Use this tool to diagnose onboarding failures. Each history entry includes: timestamp, details (summary text), errorFlag (true when the entry records a failure), and historyTaskInfo containing name (workflow step name), type (step type), and workItemList[]. Each workItem has: state, command (the operation attempted), outputStr (the actual CLI output or error message from that step), startTime, endTime. To diagnose a failure: sort by timestamp descending, find entries where errorFlag=true, then surface the historyTaskInfo.name (failed step) and workItemList[].outputStr (the exact error output) to the user. Also check historyTaskInfo.addnDetails[] for key-value pairs with additional diagnostic context.",
